  "steps": [
    "Toss the diced chicken with its seasoning (salt, pepper, paprika, oregano and garlic powder).",
    "Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium-low heat. Saute the onion a few minutes until translucent, then stir in a few pinches of salt and pepper and the 1 1/2 tbsp oregano.",
    "Raise the heat to medium. Add the chicken and garlic and cook, stirring often, about 8 min until the chicken is browned.",
    "Stir in the sun-dried tomatoes, tomato paste and paprika and cook 1-2 min.",
    "Add the cream and bone broth, cover, and bring to a simmer, 6-10 min.",
    "Add the pasta and simmer, stirring often, for the time on the package, until tender. Add a splash more broth or water if it gets too thick. The chicken should be cooked through (165°F) by now.",
    "About 2 minutes before the pasta is done, stir in the spinach and basil until wilted. Taste and adjust the salt.",
    "Serve topped with Parmesan, more basil and red pepper flakes."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "If meal prepping, leave the pasta out and cook it into the soup when reheating.",
    "The creator uses high-protein low-carb pasta that cooks in about 5 minutes; regular dried pasta takes 9-12 minutes and drinks more broth."
  ],
